search:C.summary:
No earlier report of Candidate C was found.

Every working search, each with a control that found a known object, came back empty at C's position:
- SIMBAD, through two official mirrors only, so it is not evidence: the control failed and CDS was down at all four tries;
- 25 VizieR catalogues: the VVV eruptive and high-amplitude lists, VIVACE, V4, SPICY and two YSO-variability tables, Gaia DR3 variability, ASAS-SN variables, GCVS/NSV, VSX (version 2026-10-18), eight nova catalogues and eROSITA X-ray transients;
- the Lucas and Guo 2024 VVV tables, read through arXiv HTML;
- the vsnet-alert subjects from Aug 2025 to Nov 2026;
- MAXI, Swift/BAT, the Fermi-LAT nova list, AAVSO campaigns and forum alerts, Wikipedia, and the CBET titles from Aug 2025 to Nov 2026;
- open-web searches for the J-name, the Galactic name, Nova Norma/Normae 2025 and 2026, and new Norma designations (none was assigned after V567 Nor).

Within 30 arcsec, the only entries are two variable stars catalogued before 2025: a Gaia RS-type star at 11.95 arcsec and a VVV contact binary at 15.46 arcsec. Both are periodic, low-amplitude and too far away to be C.

The two Norma X-ray events of 2025-26 are 3.5 and 5.4 deg away:
- MAXI J1543-564, Dec 2025, identity confirmed by NuSTAR;
- MAXI J1609-487, Oct 2026.
Their ATels are for a person to read. The nearest 2025-26 optical event is the HP Nor dwarf-nova outburst, 3.4 deg away.

Also left for a person: ATel full text, ADS, SIMBAD at CDS once it is back, the BAA alert archive (groups.io restricts AI access) and a few AAVSO campaign pages.

On the user's question ('the AI thing, the simulation one'): this step ran no simulation. It made real requests to real public services, 341 of them, all logged with UTC times in <scratchpad>/recheck/C/out/fetch_log.tsv . This step cannot tell what 'the simulation one' refers to; the team lead should answer that. Raw downloads are in <scratchpad>/recheck/C/dl/ and the VizieR summary in <scratchpad>/recheck/C/out/vizier_summary.txt .
